menu "WiEvac receiver"

config WIEVAC_RX_ID
    int "Receiver ID"
    range 1 64
    default 1
    help
        Logical receiver identity for this firmware image. One binary is
        flashed per RX board; IDs 1-64 are valid. Pairing and airtime for
        more than two receivers remain a transmitter schedule concern.

config WIEVAC_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID"
    default ""
    help
        Deployment SSID. Leave empty until a local deployment config is supplied.

config WIEVAC_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default ""

config WIEVAC_PI_IP
    string "Raspberry Pi IPv4 address"
    default ""

config WIEVAC_PI_UDP_PORT
    int "Raspberry Pi UDP port"
    range 1 65535
    default 8888

config WIEVAC_FORCE_RX_GAIN
    bool "Force the PHY RX gain after training (breaks the Wi-Fi uplink)"
    default n
    help
        Off by default. Forcing AGC/FFT gain makes the radio drop most frames,
        so the node loses the Pi AP within seconds. When off, AGC stays
        automatic and CSI bytes reach the pipeline raw (no in-place gain
        scaling, which clipped strong links).

config WIEVAC_BOOT_SETTLE_S
    int "Seconds to wait after power-on before computing"
    range 0 600
    default 120
    help
        Right after power-on the radio/AGC is still settling and the person
        who plugged the node in is still nearby. For this many seconds the RX
        learns nothing and publishes UNKNOWN / warming_up; the formula and the
        Tiny-AI noise reference start from the first settled frame. Leave the
        corridor empty during and for about a minute after this period.

config WIEVAC_REBASE_QUIET_S
    int "Seconds of quiet, person-free corridor before learning a new baseline"
    range 12 600
    default 30
    help
        A new empty-corridor baseline is learned only after this many seconds
        in a row with no motion, no occupancy and (with a model) no AI
        evidence. Any such window restarts the count.

config WIEVAC_RAW_CSI_UDP
    bool "Send raw CSI to the Pi (opt-in)"
    default n
    help
        Off by default. When enabled, unfiltered CSI frames are batched and
        sent as WRAW datagrams to port (base + RX id). WIV5 on the Pi port
        is unchanged.

config WIEVAC_RAW_CSI_UDP_PORT_BASE
    int "Raw CSI UDP port base"
    depends on WIEVAC_RAW_CSI_UDP
    range 1 65471
    default 8890
    help
        Destination port is this base plus CONFIG_WIEVAC_RX_ID.
        8890 sends RX-1 to 8891 and RX-2 to 8892.

config WIEVAC_EXPECTED_TX_MAC
    string "Expected transmitter Wi-Fi MAC (optional closed-lab fallback)"
    default ""
    help
        When set, only HELLO/measurement frames from this transmitter MAC are
        accepted. Leave empty only for trusted closed-lab pairing.

endmenu
